Let $X$ be a smooth variety embedded in projective space $\mathbb P^n$. Let $C$ be a closed conical subset of the cotangent space of $X$ of dimension $\dim X$. Let $x \in X$ be a point such that $C$ does not contain the cotangent space of $x$.

Let $\overline{X} \subseteq X \times \mathbb P^1$ be a general pencil of conic sections of $X$, parameterized by $\mathbb P^1$.  Let $p$ and $q$ be the natural projections in the below commutative diagram.\begin{equation}\label{pq-diagram}\text{[Diagram omitted; see source PDF.]} \end{equation}


Then $p$ is properly $C$-transversal, $q$ is $p^{\circ} C$-transversal in a neighborhood of the unique conic in the pencil containing $x$, and the fibers of $p^\circ C$ over $\mathbb P^1$ are $\dim X-1$-dimensional in a neighborhood of the conic containing $x$.
